-- Reverse migration 25.
--
-- Schema only. The data migration is deliberately not reversed, and that is a
-- choice rather than an omission:
--
-- - The recovery Notebook is left in place. Deleting it would destroy whatever
--   an operator has since added to it, and the Sources inside it were already
--   stranded once.
-- - Owner values are left on their rows. With the field definition gone they are
--   inert, and re-running the up path finds them still present and does not
--   reassign them.
-- - The admin `member` row is left alone. It belongs to migration 24, and an
--   operator may be signed in against it. Rolling back past this point is
--   migration 24's business.
--
-- Order matters: the index and the events reference the table, so they go first.
-- The events are removed before the table so that dropping `share` cannot fire
-- a cleanup against a table that is halfway gone.

REMOVE EVENT IF EXISTS share_cleanup_on_member_delete ON TABLE member;
REMOVE EVENT IF EXISTS share_cleanup_on_notebook_delete ON TABLE notebook;
REMOVE INDEX IF EXISTS share_member_notebook ON TABLE share;
REMOVE TABLE IF EXISTS share;

REMOVE INDEX IF EXISTS notebook_owner ON TABLE notebook;
REMOVE FIELD IF EXISTS owner ON TABLE notebook;
